generated_hash =

// @vibe/compiler/runtime — ADR-0070 / #897 compiler-internal contract,
// compiler-internal batch 8. Directory-shared-scope package (originally 7
// impl files, ~4275 lines; doc_at.vibe added under #854): the incremental
// type-check database (`TypeDb` + the
// db_new/db_set_source/db_check_env/db_typecheck*/db_merged_source/
// db_module_source/db_load_artifact/db_store_artifact family, runtime.vibe),
// module-source reconstruction for the debugger funcmap sidecar
// (module_source.vibe), editor-query primitives backing `vibe type-at` /
// `vibe binding-at` / `vibe symbols` / `vibe doc-at` (type_at.vibe,
// binding_at.vibe, symbol_spans.vibe, doc_at.vibe), filesystem-driven
// typecheck + diagnostics collection (typecheck_fs.vibe), and the
// persistent dep-list / type-env / leaf-fingerprint cache codec
// (persistent_env_codec.vibe).
//
// Naming: no collision on the established `git mv index.vibe <dirname>.vibe`
// convention (runtime/runtime.vibe didn't exist), same as loader/'s batch —
// the old index.vibe moved verbatim to runtime.vibe.
//
// runtime.vibe is NOT a pure facade — like loader.vibe's and
// checker_facade.vibe's siblings, it carries substantial real implementation
// of its own (the whole `TypeDb` incremental-cache state machine) in
// addition to importing and re-exporting a hand-picked subset of its
// siblings' surfaces via existing `export ./file.vibe { .. }` SReExport
// blocks (module_source.vibe, type_at.vibe, binding_at.vibe,
// symbol_spans.vibe, typecheck_fs.vibe — added under #847). Those blocks
// stay untouched: this contract is now the actual source of truth for the
// package's full export surface (all names below, across all 7 files), so
// runtime.vibe's partial, hand-picked re-export list is no longer
// load-bearing for outside callers — they reach every name here through
// this contract regardless of what runtime.vibe itself re-exports, exactly
// like checker_facade.vibe's and loader.vibe's partial lists after their
// own batches.
//
// Two-level SReExport nesting wrinkle: typecheck_fs.vibe is itself a
// substantial-impl file (933 lines: locate_type_error,
// ensure_fingerprint_fs_impl, check_inline_wasm_fns,
// collect_all_diagnostics) carrying its OWN `export ./persistent_env_codec.vibe
// { .. }` SReExport block — one level deeper than loader/'s shape, where
// only the top-level facade had the SReExport pattern, not a sibling too.
// This turned out not to matter for the contract: `contract_sibling_impl_raws`
// directory auto-discovery reaches persistent_env_codec.vibe directly
// regardless of what re-exports what, so its 6 exports below are declared
// straight from its own file grouping, exactly as if typecheck_fs.vibe's
// SReExport didn't exist. Verified empirically via
// scripts/unit_test_runner.sh (full run), not just assumed.
//
// `export let`-bound functions: module_source.vibe's two exports are
// `export let name: (Params) -> Ret with Exception = (params) -> { .. }`
// bindings, not `export fn`. No other already-migrated vpkg contract had
// this exact shape (checked via `grep -rn '^export let .*-> .* with '`;
// the pattern used to end in `with {` — #1429 removed the braces)
// across every migrated directory — no hits besides this one). Confirmed
// this still fingerprints as an ordinary fn signature for
// `collect_impl_fn_defs`/`check_contract`: the parser's
// `apply_generic_fn_annotation` (lib/@vibe/parser/parser_expr.vibe) injects
// the let annotation's declared return type and effect row into the
// lambda's own `EFn` node when the lambda itself doesn't specify them, so
// the contract can declare both plain `fn name(params) -> Ret with Exception`
// below exactly like every `export fn` — no special contract syntax needed.
//
// No exported types besides `TypeDb`: TypeEnv/Stmt/Type/Expr (../core) are
// plain structural signature text here, not declared at all (checker/
// loader/ precedent — ../core itself is not yet migrated to vpkg, out of
// scope for this batch); RippleDb (../../../../lib/@vibe/graph) is likewise
// left undeclared, already covered by graph's own contract. `TypeDb` itself
// is declared `opaque`: its real definition wraps a private `TypeDbState`
// payload (itself wrapping private `StringTriple` — neither is `export`ed
// in runtime.vibe, so neither needs a contract entry at all), and no
// consumer (in-repo, confirmed via repo-wide grep) ever constructs or
// pattern-matches a `TypeDb` directly, only through db_new/db_set_source/
// db_check_env/... — same precedent as graph.vpkg's opaque `RippleDb`.
//
// External-caller fixes (literal `runtime/index.vibe` /
// `runtime/typecheck_fs.vibe` paths → bare `../runtime` / `./runtime`
// package form, now that leaf-file imports from outside the package are
// rejected by enforce_incoming_boundary_fs): cli_adapter.vibe,
// cli_support.vibe (was importing check_inline_wasm_fns/locate_type_error
// straight from typecheck_fs.vibe — neither is re-exported by runtime.vibe's
// own facade block, but both are covered here so the package-form import
// still resolves), entry/compiler/fs_compile/index.vibe,
// entry/compiler/file_compile/file_compile.vibe,
// entry/cli_cache/cli_cache.vibe. No import cycle found: none of runtime/'s
// own dependencies (checker/, codegen/, loader/, syntax/, cache/
// persistent_cache.vibe, ../../../../lib/@vibe/graph — all already vpkg or
// plain leaf imports of non-vpkg directories) import back into runtime/;
// loader/ imports `../runtime/eval_loader` (a distinct, already-migrated
// subpackage), never this directory's own index.vpkg/runtime.vibe.
//
// Compiled into the compiler itself via compiler_sources_manifest.tsv
// (group `runtime`): the old single `runtime/index.vibe` row becomes a
// dual row (this contract + runtime/runtime.vibe); typecheck_fs.vibe,
// type_at.vibe, binding_at.vibe, symbol_spans.vibe,
// persistent_env_codec.vibe, module_source.vibe already had their own rows
// and are unchanged.

// --- runtime.vibe
